.TH LIELLA-GCC 1 "" "Liella" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liella-gcc, liella-g++ \- build programs that run on the Liella C library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liella-gcc
.RI [ gcc-options ] " file" ...
.br
.B liella-g++
.RI [ g++-options ] " file" ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B liella-gcc
runs the system's
.BR gcc (1)
(\fBliella-g++\fR: \fBg++\fR(1)).
Compiling (\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-S\fR, \fB\-E\fR, \fB\-M\fR, \fB\-MM\fR) is unchanged and uses
the system's C headers.
A link uses only Liella's start files and libraries from the sysroot
.I /usr/lib/liella
and sets the program interpreter to
.IR /usr/lib/liella/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 ,
so the program runs on Liella; the system's C library is not used.
.PP
\fB\-static\fR links Liella's static library; \fB\-shared\fR builds a shared object
against Liella.
\fBliella-g++\fR links the C++ library and the unwinder statically.
The loader's default library search is the sysroot only: a program that needs another
system library names its directory with \fB\-Wl,\-rpath,\fR\fIdir\fR.
\fB\-static\-pie\fR and \fB\-pg\fR are refused.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIELLA_REAL_CC\fR, \fBLIELLA_REAL_CXX
The compilers (default \fBgcc\fR and \fBg++\fR).
.TP
.B LIELLA_SYSROOT
Where the link-time files are read from (default \fI/usr/lib/liella\fR).
The program interpreter is always the installed loader.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gcc (1),
.BR ld (1)
